@NODE INTRODUCTION "INTRODUCTION OF COECP V1.1"

COECP V1.1 IS NOT ONLY ANOTHER NEW SYSOP PAGER. IT HAS @{"FEATURES" LINK FEATURES} THAT OTHER 
PAGERS DOESN'T HAVE. YOU SHOULD NOT REPLACE COECP V1.0 WITH YOUR OLD PAGER.
LET IT RUN BESIDE YOUR OLD PAGER JUST WITH ANOTHER COMMAND TO START IT.
SET THE CHAT-OVERRIDE-LEVEL TO AN AMMOUNT THAT EVERY USER IS ABLE TO PAGE
YOU AT ANY TIME. 

THE USER HAS TO PAY WITH HIS CREDITS IF HE WANTS TO PAGE THE SYSOP AND HE
WILL DO THIS ONLY IF THERE IS SOMETHING REALLY IMPORTANT. SO, NEVER WILL
PAGE THE SYSOP JUST FOR FUN AND THE SYSOP CAN BE PAGED AT EVERY TIME.  

@ENDNODE

@NODE FEATURES "FEATURES OF COECP V1.1"

COECP V1.1 LOOKS HOW MANY UPLOAD BYTES THE USER WHO WANTS TO PAGE THE SYSOP
HAS AND CALCULATES HOW MANY BEEPS THE USER CAN USE. IF THE USER HAS ACCESS
TO THE FREE-MODE HE DOES NOT HAVE TO PAY FOR HIS BEEPS. THE AMMOUNT HOW MUCH
A BEEP DOES COST, WHICH USERS HAVE ACCESS TO THE FREE-MODE AND HOW HIGH IS
THE CHAT-OVERIDE-LEVEL ARE IN THE @{"CONFIGFILES" LINK CONFIGFILES}.

AFTER THE USER PAGED THE SYSOP COECP V1.1 CALCULATES THE NEW AMMOUNT OF
CREDITS THE USER HAS LEFT (IS SHOWN TO THE USER) AND STORES THIS TO HIS
USERDATA.

@ENDNODE

@NODE INSTALLATION "INSTALLATION OF COECP V1.1"

INSTALLATION TO @{"AMI EXPRESS V2.xx" LINK AMIEXPRESSV2.xx}.

INSTALLATION TO @{"AMI EXPRESS V3.xx" LINK AMIEXPRESSV3.xx}.

@ENDNODE

@NODE AMIEXPRESSV2.xx "INSTALLATION TO AMI EXPRESS V2.xx"

TO INSTALL THE DOOR LOAD UP THE CUSTOMCOMMANDS (/X V2.2x OR BELOW) OR
BBS.CMD (/X V2.3x) AND ADD THE FOLLOWING LINE TO THE LIST.


          11 SPACES IN         
          |
-----------------------------------------------          
*PAGE     RM010MODULES:ABSTURZ/COECP/COECP.REXX
-----------------------------------------------
||        |||  |           
||        |||  ` 'MODULES:ABSTURZ/COECP/COECP.REXX' IS THE LOCATION OF
||        |||     THE FILE.
||        |||
||        ||` 020 THE MINIMUM ACCESS TO USE THIS DOOR. CHANGE IT TO WHAT
||        ||      YOU LIKE.
||        ||
||        |` 'M' FOR A MULTINODE BBS ('S' FOR A SINGLE NODE BBS).
||        |
||        ` 'R' FOR A REXX DOOR WHICH WILL USE THE 'REXXDOOR'-UTIL.
||
|`COMMAND TO START THE DOOR.
|
`-RETARD OPTION. TO MAKE SURE THEY ONLY USE 'S' & ONLY  'S' TO GET THE
  DOOR TO COME UP. IF NOT USED, THINGS SUCH AS 'START' AND 'SA' WOULD
  STILL BRING UP THE DOOR.


  USE THE LINE BETWEEN THE LINES ONLY. THE OTHER PARTS ARE JUST AN
  EXPLANATION TO MAKE SURE YOU KNOW WHAT EACH PART IS DOING (SINCE
  NOONE WOULD TELL ME BACK IN THE DAYS WHERE I DIDN'T KNOW WHAT WAS
  GOING ON!)  

  NOW COPY THE DIRECTORY 'MODULES' FROM THE LHA-ARCHIEV TO YOUR BBS.

  AT LAST EDIT THE @{"CONFIGFILES" LINK CONFIGFILES}. YOU FIND WILL THEM IN
 
  'BBS:MODULES/ABSTURZ/COECP'.

@ENDNODE

@NODE AMIEXPRESSV3.xx "INSTALLATION TO AMI EXPRESS V3.xx"

YOU ONLY NEED TO COPY THE FILES FROM THE LHA-ARCHIEVE TO YOUR BBS. THEN
EDIT THE @{"CONFIGFILES" LINK CONFIGFILES}. YOU WILL FIND THEM IN 'BBS:MODULES/ABSTURZ/COECP'.

@ENDNODE

@NODE CONFIGFILES "HOW TO EDIT THE CONFIGFILES?"

1. CREDITSPAGE.NAMES
 
   - THIS IS THE LIST OF USER'S NAMES WHO HAVE ACCESS TO THE FREE-MODE.
     
     E.G.:

     - Line 1 = MuMu
     - Line 2 = HELiON
     - Line 3 = SPIDER


     ALL USERS IN THIS LIST DO NOT HAVE TO PAY IF THEY WANT TO PAGE THE
     SYSOP. 

     CAN ADD AS MANY USERS AS YOU WANT TO.


2. CREDITSPAGE.CFG

   - Line 1 = 20      <- CHAT-OVERIDE-LEVEL
   - Line 2 = 102400  <- AMMOUNT HOW MUCH A BEEP DOES COST
   - Line 3 = 10      <- THE MAXIMUM NUMBER OF BEEPS THE COECP V1.0 WILL
                         DO, IF THE USER HAS ENOUGH CREDITS  

@ENDNODE       

